-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
-- Reviewed value comparisons, schema 1. tools/verb_registry_gate.mix reads this file.
--
-- A value comparison is a verb compared with a runtime value: neither operand is a string
-- literal or a resolvable constant, so the gate cannot name the verb it compares. Every such
-- comparison must be listed here, or the gate reports it as an unreviewed value comparison.
-- An entry that matches no site is a stale exemption, also a violation.
--
-- Each entry has four keys:
--   file    the path, relative to the repo root, as the gate reports it;
--   fn      the enclosing function, NAME or Type::NAME for a method in an impl block. The
--           entry binds only a site whose enclosing fn AND text both match. Two matching
--           sites are an ambiguous exemption, and the gate fails closed;
--   text    the comparison as the gate normalises it: the left operand, the operator and
--           the right operand, one space each side (a method form reads `x.eq(y)`). Line
--           numbers are not part of an entry, so a site moves with its code;
--   reason  why the comparison is safe. It is read by the reviewer, not the gate.
--
-- The optional trusted_macros list (round 29) names the macros a file may invoke at item or
-- statement position and still resolve its constants. Each entry has two keys:
--   name    the macro's name, a plain identifier (println, info); the path prefix must be one
--           of std::, core::, alloc::, tracing::, log:: or none (the gate reads the prefix);
--   reason  why the macro declares no item and cannot hide a constant. Read by the reviewer.
-- An invocation of any other macro, a macro_rules! definition, a #[macro_use], or a use that
-- can rebind one of these names makes its file's constants unreadable (fail closed). Adding an
-- entry is a reviewer decision: the gate reports the unreadable sites, and the list is not
-- widened to make a tree pass.
--
-- The optional test_doubles list names a fake service, a file compiled only for tests. Each
-- entry has two keys (round 21):
--   file    the path, relative to the repo root, as the gate reports it;
--   reason  why the file is a test double. It is read by the reviewer, not the gate.
-- The file is scanned like any other file: every registration in it is checked, so an
-- unregistered, retired or badly named verb in it still fails, and its declarations and parse
-- arms are checked for owner and declared_by in full (round 22). Its answers are not an owner,
-- though: they create no owner-conflict and count for no coverage, so a verb that only the
-- double answers is not-in-code for its registered owner. The gate does not read cfg or
-- module declarations, so an entry says nothing about where the file is compiled.
-- An entry whose file is missing, or holds no answering site, is stale-test-double and
-- applies to nothing. An answering site is a dispatch, prefix, guard, route row, Mix on handler
-- or variant handler; a declaration alone is not one, so a declaration-only file is stale.
--
-- The optional request_builders list names a site that BUILDS a request for a verb, rather than
-- answering it: the client side of a verb whose answer lives in another component. Each entry
-- has five keys:
--   file    as above;
--   fn      as above: the enclosing fn of the site. The entry binds only a site whose fn and
--           text both match; two matching sites are an ambiguous exemption;
--   text    the site's exact normalised keep-view source, as the gate reads it: a `match <expr> {`
--           head (the entry covers the listed verbs' arms in that match only), a comparison
--           `LHS == "verb"` (matched exactly), or a tuple expression (`("verb", body)`);
--   verbs   the verbs the site builds requests for. Each must be registered, concrete or by
--           family, or the entry is an unregistered-request violation. A listed verb at the site
--           contributes no answer; an arm for an unlisted verb in a keyed match still counts;
--   reason  why the site only builds requests. It is read by the reviewer, not the gate.
-- An entry that matches no site in its file and fn is a stale request builder, also a violation.
-- A `match <expr> {` head is keyed only when <expr> is a dispatch scrutinee (verb, command, cmd,
-- method or command_name()). A match on any other expression, such as `match self {`, is never
-- read as dispatch: its arms are not read, so it needs no entry and an entry for it is stale.
-- The gate reads an arm's pattern (the left of `=>`), never its value: `Op::List => "releases.list"`
-- records nothing. A dispatch arm `"verb" => ...` does record its literal pattern.
{
  schema: 1,
  exemptions: [
    {file:"services/noded/src/session.rs", "fn":"Sessions::execute", text:"cached.command == request.command", reason:"replay cache equality: a stored command is compared with the incoming one; equal means replay and unequal is a Conflict. Both sides are runtime values and no verb is dispatched from the comparison."},
    {file:"apps/busviewer/crates/inspector/src/model.rs", "fn":"Snapshot::verb", text:"v.name == selection.verb", reason:"selection lookup: finds the verb whose name is the selected one and returns an Option. A miss is an absent selection, not a dispatch."},
    {file:"services/editd/src/router.rs", "fn":"Editd::route", text:"*v == verb", reason:"membership before dispatch: the requested verb is looked up in the VERBS table, whose declarations and dispatch arms the gate scans. An unknown verb is refused and never dispatched."},
    {file:"libs/bus/src/native_client/native.rs", "fn":"NodedClient::session_request", text:"response.command_name() != Some(command)", reason:"response envelope echo check: a native-session client validates that the reply names the command it sent (alongside bus, native-session, type, id, rc); not dispatch."}
  ],
  test_doubles: [
    {file:"libs/editor-model/src/fake.rs", reason:"fake editd for editor-model mirror tests; compiled only under test or the fake feature"}
  ],
  request_builders: [
    {file:"libs/editor-model/src/mirror.rs", "fn":"Mirror::send_server", text:'verb == "edit.save"', verbs:["edit.save"], reason:"editor-model mirror client: builds outgoing edit.* request bodies; editd answers"},
    {file:"libs/editor-model/src/mirror.rs", "fn":"Mirror::resend", text:'wire.verb == "edit.save"', verbs:["edit.save"], reason:"editor-model mirror client: builds outgoing edit.* request bodies; editd answers"},
    {file:"libs/editor-model/src/mirror.rs", "fn":"Mirror::server_body", text:"match verb {", verbs:["edit.insert", "edit.delete"], reason:"editor-model mirror client: builds outgoing edit.* request bodies; editd answers"},
    {file:"libs/editor-model/src/mirror.rs", "fn":"Mirror::server_body", text:'("edit.save", body)', verbs:["edit.save"], reason:"editor-model mirror client: builds outgoing edit.* request bodies; editd answers"},
    {file:"apps/prefs/src/shell.rs", "fn":"budget", text:"match verb {", verbs:["releases.list", "releases.notes", "releases.status", "releases.check"], reason:"Prefs releases call budget: a timeout per releases.* verb it sends; releasesd answers"}
  ],
  trusted_macros: [
    {name:"println", reason:"std: prints to stdout; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"print", reason:"std: prints to stdout; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"eprintln", reason:"std: prints to stderr; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"eprint", reason:"std: prints to stderr; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"format", reason:"std: builds a String; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"format_args", reason:"std: builds fmt::Arguments; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"write", reason:"std: writes formatted text to a writer; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"writeln", reason:"std: writes formatted text and a newline to a writer; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"vec", reason:"std: builds a Vec; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"assert", reason:"std: panics when its condition is false; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"assert_eq", reason:"std: panics when two values differ; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"assert_ne", reason:"std: panics when two values are equal; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"debug_assert", reason:"std: assert in debug builds; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"debug_assert_eq", reason:"std: assert_eq in debug builds; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"debug_assert_ne", reason:"std: assert_ne in debug builds; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"panic", reason:"std: diverges with a message; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"unreachable", reason:"std: diverges; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"todo", reason:"std: diverges; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"unimplemented", reason:"std: diverges; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"matches", reason:"std: tests a value against a pattern; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"dbg", reason:"std: prints and returns its value; expands to an expression, declares no item"},
    {name:"error", reason:"tracing or log: an error-level log call; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"warn", reason:"tracing or log: a warn-level log call; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"info", reason:"tracing or log: an info-level log call; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"debug", reason:"tracing or log: a debug-level log call; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"trace", reason:"tracing or log: a trace-level log call; expands to a statement, declares no item"},
    {name:"log", reason:"log crate: a generic log call; expands to a statement, declares no item"}
  ]
}
